# {{.project_name}}

Tool-using agent application generated from the AAI platform template
(`agent-app`, successor of `agentic-rag`'s agent half): governed prompt, SDK
tool-execution loop, structured outputs, tracing, trajectory-aware offline
evaluation, feedback, and a gated Model Serving deployment.

## Local setup

Before generation, complete the platform's developer onboarding checklist.
Then run the generated preflight and setup:

```bash
python3.12 scripts/setup_dev.py
make check
```

Run `make help` for individual development, evaluation, and bundle targets.

Use `python3.12 scripts/setup_dev.py --check-only` to verify tools,
authentication, SDK volume access, and compute-policy visibility without
installing anything. The setup never grants permissions or creates cloud
resources.

Replace every `replace-with-*` value in `aai-platform.yml` before running a
provider integration.

## How the agent works

- `src/app/tools.py` registers code tools (plain Python) in a
  `ToolRegistry`; for governed structured-data lookups, create Unity
  Catalog functions and list them in `UC_FUNCTION_TOOLS` so deployment
  declares them as serving resources.
- `src/app/agent.py` drives `aai_core.agents.run_tool_loop` (bounded turns,
  every invocation recorded) and finishes with
  `aai_core.structured.generate_structured` for a schema-validated final
  answer (`src/app/schemas.py`).
- Tests script the model's tool calls with
  `aai_core.testing.FakeChatModel(tool_call_script=...)` — fully hermetic.

## Release lifecycle

1. Edit `prompts/system_prompt.json`; register a version:
   `python scripts/register_prompt.py`.
2. Grow `evals/data/release_cases.json` — every case declares
   `expected_tools`, including no-tool cases, so trajectory regressions
   (missing lookups OR gratuitous extra calls) fail the gate.
3. Run the gate: `python evals/evaluate.py` — Correctness/Safety judges plus
   deterministic `tool_call_accuracy` from the recorded trajectories, with
   the thresholds in `evals/gate_config.json` and baseline regression;
   report published to the CI summary. After a released run:
   `--update-baseline`.
   After case changes merge, register the ground truth in Unity Catalog:
   `python scripts/sync_dataset.py` — evaluation runs link the dataset
   by name.
4. Promote the prompt (`python scripts/promote_prompt.py --version <n>
   --to candidate|production`).
5. Deploy — only after the gate passes:
   `python scripts/deploy_serving.py` logs the models-from-code wrapper
   (use `--register-only` to register the agent as code in Unity Catalog
   without deploying an endpoint)
   (`serving/model.py`) with its resource declarations, registers it in
   Unity Catalog, and deploys via Model Serving with scale-to-zero.
6. Enable production monitoring from `notebooks/02_enable_monitoring.py`
   (sampled scorers are Beta and notebook-only) and attach user feedback to
   traces; curate real failures back into the release cases.

Pull-request CI runs only the deterministic checks
(`evals/offline_checks.py`) — it never holds credentials. The platform team
must onboard this repository (main-branch federated credential, service
principal, constrained compute, serving permissions for the deploy step,
non-secret repository variables) before the deploy workflow is enabled.
